@startuml sourcing-workflow

' ============================================================
' VISUAL THEME
' ============================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam ArrowColor #57606A
skinparam DefaultFontName "SansSerif"
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF

skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ParticipantBorderColor #57606A
  LifeLineBorderColor #57606A
  GroupBackgroundColor #F6F8FA
  GroupBorderColor #57606A
}
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8C5
skinparam noteBorderColor #57606A

title ITIP Definition Blackboard Repository Sourcer - Sourcing workflow (single-Blackboard Run; client-side choreography over the Definition Blackboard Manager REST substrate)

' ---- Client side (ITIP-specific) ----
participant "ITIP Sourcer\n(RunDriver + RepoBootstrap)" as RD
participant "KSs (discovery / lift\n+ GSM-spine; client-internal,\nsandboxed)" as KSs
participant "External tools\n(scip-*, syft, tokei,\njoern-parse)" as ExtT
participant "Inference service\n(LLM)" as Inf
participant "DefMan exploration\nclient" as DefExp
participant "Schema validator\n(client-side)" as JV
participant "Client BundleStore\n(working copy + tool outputs)" as BS
participant "Client Reducer\n(controller-side)" as Red
participant "Post-reduction pipeline\n(validate + register to DefMan)" as PIPE

' ---- Substrate side (Definition Blackboard Manager) ----
participant "REST API" as API
participant "Blackboard\nManager" as BBMgr
participant "Panel Registry" as PanelReg
participant "Contribution\nValidator" as Val
participant "Seal Manager" as Seal
database    "Blackboard\nStore + Audit" as Store

note over RD, Store
  **Scope** -- one client Run = one Blackboard.

  This diagram merges two views in a single sequence:
   * the **client-side ITIP choreography** (RunDriver, KSs, external
     tools, inference, reducer, post-reduction pipeline);
   * the **substrate-side REST sequence** (API, Blackboard Manager,
     Panel Registry, Contribution Validator, Seal Manager, Store).

  Each "Client posts ..." round-trip exposes the substrate's internal
  participants so both layers are visible. The substrate has NO
  Run/Phase/chaining/correlation concept; each Blackboard is fully
  isolated. `runId` and the DAG between KSs are purely client-side.

  Panels (client-declared, see `panels.puml`):
  - `itip:SourceInventory`, `itip:SourceUnit`,
    `itip:SourceRelation`, `itip:SourceInterface`
  - `itip:Definition`, `itip:Archetype`, `itip:Statement`

  KS catalogue:
  - Discovery / lift: `RepoInventoryKS`, `ScipIngestKS`,
    `ConfigInterfaceKS`, `JoernCallGraphKS`, `InterfaceLiftKS`
  - GSM-spine:        `GsmIdentificationKS`, `GsmReconciliationKS`,
                      `ArchetypeMatchingKS`, `StatementShapingKS`,
                      `GranularityKS` (TOP_DOWN), `ConfidenceSynthesisKS`
end note

== Blackboard creation ==

RD -> RD : mint runId (client-side)
RD -> API : POST /blackboards\n  BlackboardConfig { name: "<repoLabel>",\n    auth: { writerSubjects: [...], bbAdminSubjects: [...] } }
API -> BBMgr : create Blackboard
BBMgr -> Store : persist Blackboard\n(status=OPEN, timestamp)
BBMgr --> API : 201 + bbId + ETag
API --> RD : 201 bbId, ETag

RD -> RD : RepoBootstrap.clone(gitUrl, ref)\n  -> working copy in BundleStore
RD -> RD : derive scope (include/exclude globs)\n  + profile

== Declare topology (before first contribution) ==

RD -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/panels\n  PanelDeclaration[] (7 panels: 4 itip:Source* + 3 GSM-spine,\n  single DAG)\n  If-Match: <ETag>
API -> PanelReg : register panels
PanelReg -> PanelReg : validate client-namespacing\n  + per-slot schemaUri form
PanelReg -> Store : persist panels + slots
PanelReg --> API : 201 + panelIds + ETag
API --> RD : 200 (DAG validated, schema URIs cached), new ETag

note right of PanelReg
  Topology is **frozen** when the first
  contribution is accepted. A subsequent
  POST .../panels then returns 409.
end note

== Run loop (client-side scheduling over the single DAG) ==

loop until quiescence OR client-side maxIterations

  RD -> API : GET /blackboards/{bbId}/state  (current view)
  API -> Store : read view
  API --> RD : state
  RD -> RD : enumerate eligible KSs\n(triggerPredicate true)

  RD -> KSs : fire eligible KSs (client-internal)

  alt RepoInventoryKS fires (BOTTOM_UP)
    KSs -> ExtT : execve tokei / syft (sandboxed)
    ExtT -> BS : write tool outputs
    ExtT --> KSs : output handles
    KSs -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (contributionSlot={panel:itip:SourceInventory,\n     slot=FileTreeNode | GitCommit | ModuleSpec | LanguageClassification | FileMetrics | SbomComponent},\n   post={...})

  else ScipIngestKS fires (BOTTOM_UP)
    KSs -> ExtT : execve scip-{java|typescript|python|go} (sandboxed)
    ExtT -> BS : write SCIP index
    ExtT --> KSs : SCIP index handle
    KSs -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (panel=itip:SourceUnit, slot=CodeUnit, ...)
    KSs -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (panel=itip:SourceRelation,\n   slot=SymbolRef | TypeHierarchyEdge | ImplementationEdge | ImportEdge, ...)

  else ConfigInterfaceKS fires (BOTTOM_UP)
    KSs -> API : GET /blackboards/{bbId}/state  (live itip:SourceInventory view)
    KSs -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (panel=itip:SourceInventory, slot=ConfigEntry, ...)
    KSs -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (panel=itip:SourceInterface,\n   slot=OpenApiOperation | KafkaTopic | DbTable, ...)

  else JoernCallGraphKS fires (BOTTOM_UP)
    KSs -> API : GET /blackboards/{bbId}/state  (live itip:SourceUnit view)
    KSs -> ExtT : execve joern-parse / joern-export (sandboxed)
    ExtT -> BS : write CPG outputs
    ExtT --> KSs : CPG handle
    KSs -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (panel=itip:SourceRelation, slot=CallEdge | DataflowEdge, ...)

  else InterfaceLiftKS fires (BOTTOM_UP)
    KSs -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (contributionSlot={panel:itip:SourceInterface, slot:...},\n   post={..., evidence:[...]})

  else GsmIdentificationKS fires (BOTTOM_UP)
    KSs -> API : GET /blackboards/{bbId}/state  (live itip:Source* views)
    KSs -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (contributionSlot={panel:itip:Definition, slot:Claim},\n   post={subjectKind, identityKey, supportingSourceIds, ...},\n   derivedContribution=[bb://itip/blackboard/SourceInterface/.../#contrib/...])

  else GsmReconciliationKS fires (BOTTOM_UP)
    KSs -> API : GET /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (filter: panel=itip:Definition, slot=Claim, peers)
    KSs -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (panel=itip:Definition, slot=Merge,\n   post={supersedesIdentityKeys[...], targetIdentityKey})

  else ArchetypeMatchingKS fires (BOTTOM_UP)
    KSs -> API : GET /blackboards/{bbId}/state  (live itip:Definition view)
    KSs -> DefExp : navigate DefMan archetypes (read-only)
    KSs -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (panel=itip:Archetype, slot=Application,\n   post={archetypeRef})

  else StatementShapingKS fires (BOTTOM_UP)
    KSs -> API : GET /blackboards/{bbId}/state  (live itip:Archetype view)
    alt LLM-driven
      KSs -> Inf : completeStatement(identity)
      Inf --> KSs : InferenceResult\n  (carry cacheKey for deterministic replay)
    else deterministic
      KSs -> KSs : structural extraction from\n  resolved itip:Source* views
    end
    KSs -> JV : incremental archetype-schema check (client-side)
    KSs -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (panel=itip:Statement, slot=Draft,\n   post={statement, completeness, shapingMethod, evidence:[...]})

  else GranularityKS fires (TOP_DOWN)
    KSs -> API : GET /blackboards/{bbId}/state  (live itip:Statement view + peer identities)
    KSs -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (panel=itip:Definition, slot=Verdict,\n   post={verdict:keep|drop|splitInto|mergeWith, ...})

  else ConfidenceSynthesisKS fires
    KSs -> API : GET /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (panel=itip:Statement, identity, NOT resolved -- needs diversity)
    KSs -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (panel=itip:Statement, slot=Draft,\n   post={...synthesised confidence + aggregated evidence})
  end

  note over API, Store
    Substrate-side handling of every contributions POST above:
      API -> Val : validate(post vs slot.schemaUri,
                            status=OPEN,
                            derivedContribution[] same-Bb)
      alt accepted
        Val -> Store : append contribution (timestamp)
                    + audit-ledger entry (POSTED)
        Val --> API : 201 + contributionId
      else schema fail / cross-Bb derived URI
        Val --> API : 422 + diagnostics (NOT persisted)
      else blackboard not OPEN
        Val --> API : 409
      end
  end note
end

== Seal (client asserts done) ==

RD -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/seal\n  Authorization: Bearer <bb:seal scope>\n  If-Match: <ETag>
API -> Seal : transition Blackboard -> SEALING
Seal -> Store : reject further writes (409)
Seal -> Store : freeze contribution stream\n(byte-stable order:\npanel, slot, timestamp, id)
Seal -> Store : audit: seal event
Seal -> Store : Blackboard -> SEALED (sealTimestamp)
Seal --> API : 200 + sealTimestamp
API --> RD : 200 (status=SEALED)

== Read sealed contribution stream + reduce + register (client-side) ==

RD -> API : GET /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  ?panel=&slot=  (paginated;\n  byte-stable on SEALED Bb)
API -> Store : load sealed stream slice
API --> RD : Contribution[] (sealed stream slice)
RD -> Red : reduce per (panel, slot, identityKey)\n  using per-slot client policy\n  (highestConfidence / collectAll / compose / ...);\n  log (reducerId, version, params, inputContributionURIs[],\n       outputValue) for replay
Red --> RD : reducedView
RD -> PIPE : validate(reducedView) + register(Ascriptions)\n  to Definition Manager

note over PIPE
  Client-side. The substrate has no knowledge of "Ascription",
  "Definition Manager", or any GSM construct beyond opaque slot
  values. Reduction (winner / merge / compose per slot) is itself
  a client-controller process; the substrate provides only the
  byte-stable sealed contribution stream as the replay anchor.
  Validation against archetype schemas and registration to
  Definition Manager are entirely client-side concerns.

  Optional: the client MAY post terminal contributions on a
  `<client>:Resolved.*` panel BEFORE seal so the reduction output
  is itself a first-class auditable Bb citizen. The substrate
  enforces no cardinality; the client reducer decides per-slot
  single-/many-valuedness.

  Auditors can replay the entire client Run via
  `GET /blackboards/{bbId}/audit` plus the client's reducer
  process log.
end note

== Blackboard isolation (no chaining) ==

note over RD, API
  Each Blackboard is **fully isolated** on the substrate side. If
  a client flow needs another stage, the client creates another
  Blackboard independently and feeds it from the prior reducedView
  client-side and out-of-band. The substrate exposes no
  inter-Blackboard relation; `Contribution.derivedContribution[]`
  MUST reference contributions in the SAME Blackboard (cross-Bb
  URIs are rejected with 422). Cross-Bb lineage is recorded in the
  client's own log, not in the substrate.
end note

@enduml
